#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# pfaffian_det

#% text
# `pfaffian_det(m)` gives the Pfaffian of the antisymmetric matrix `m`, a polynomial in its entries whose square is `det(m)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The Pfaffian of a matrix of odd size is 0.

#% item
# The matrix must satisfy `m + transpose(m) == 0`; other matrices stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
pfaffian_det([[0, 3, 2, 1], [-3, 0, 5, 6], [-2, -5, 0, 4], [-1, -6, -4, 0]])
#% output
#= 5

#% cell
pfaffian_det([[0, a], [-a, 0]])
#% output
#= a

#% cell
pfaffian_det([[0, im], [-im, 0]])
#% output
#= im

#% cell
pfaffian_det([[0, 1, 2], [-1, 0, 3], [-2, -3, 0]])
#% output
#= 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `det`
